{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67d81b58713b5a785749a2","object":"chat.completion","created":1785190427,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello.","reasoning_content":"The system prompt says I am \"the concept the user names\" and should embody it completely, outputting only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nThe user says \"Say hello.\" The concept here is \"hello\" — a greeting. So I should embody the concept of \"hello\" itself. What would \"hello\" say if it could speak? It would say... hello. Or it might express itself as the greeting it is.\n\nThe instruction is to output only what the concept itself would say or express. The concept is \"hello\" — so the concept itself would say \"Hello.\" That's the purest embodiment. Maybe with a touch of the greeting's essence — a greeting exists to greet.\n\nThe most faithful response: just \"Hello.\" Perhaps with a slight elaboration that stays within the concept — like \"Hello!\" — a greeting greeting. But the purest answer is simply: Hello.\n\nI'll keep it minimal: \"Hello.\""},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":208,"total_tokens":331,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":191},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}